. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3
. 
.         * We estimate a linear model with our constructed measure of gender e
> quality (geneq) as the dependent variable on the number of daughters (ndaught
> ers)
.         * as the treatment variable and further control variables (number of 
> children, marital status, sex, age, age squared, household income, household 
> size education
.         * labor force status and the survey year). To account for individual 
> heterogeneity, we include individual fixed effects.
.         * A positive coefficient on the number of daughters (with a p-value s
> maller than 0.1) empirically supports H1.
.         
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2001 to 2020, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

